  "cause_linux_client": "entering ONLINE GAME the client creates a TCP socket and binds 127.0.0.1:12345 itself (as the original does in either role); in the container's own port space that bind succeeds, so dialling 127.0.0.1:12345 connected to its own socket (connect returned 0 at once) and the client then waited in a blocking recv for a greeting that never came. In every other pairing the client's bind fails because the host or a forwarder (adb, OrbStack) already holds the port. Two machines on a network never meet this: a client dials the host's address, not its own",
